  "summary": "QUERY PLAN (candidate 2): grain = one row per distinct product that has at least one perishable supply. Measures: none, this is a filtered lookup. Dimensions: product display name, supply display name. Filter: s.is_perishable_supply = true. Join path: first collapse order_items (oi) to a distinct product_id/product_name grain in a CTE (dp) to remove any order-item-level fan-out risk before joining, then INNER JOIN supplies (s) to dp on the explicit shared key s.product_id = dp.product_id — this makes the supplies relation the primary driving table and the join key fully explicit rather than relying on DISTINCT after a wide join. Outcome: Review SQL preview — alternate candidate to the initial query, using the same grounded relations (supplies, order_items) and product_id join key from the supplied metadata, but pre-deduplicating order_items to product grain before the join for a more direct, fan-out-safe join path.",
  "sql": "WITH dp AS (SELECT DISTINCT oi.product_id AS product_id, oi.product_name AS product_name FROM jaffle_shop.dev.order_items oi) SELECT dp.product_name AS product_name, s.supply_name AS supply_name FROM jaffle_shop.dev.supplies s JOIN dp ON s.product_id = dp.product_id WHERE s.is_perishable_supply = true ORDER BY dp.product_name LIMIT 100",
  "viz": "table",
  "outputs": ["product_name", "supply_name"],
  "dql": {
    "entity": "supplies",
    "dimensions": ["product_name", "supply_name"],
    "filters": ["is_perishable_supply = true"]
  }
}
